  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "title_markdown": "For $\\vec{a} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{b} = 2\\hat{i} + 0\\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$, the scalar (dot) product $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}$ is:",
      "instruction": "Choose the one correct option.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 1,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "$4$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "$2$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "$6$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$8$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q1_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Rule — dot product.** $$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = a_x b_x + a_y b_y + a_z b_z.$$\n\n**Step 1 — Multiply matching components.** $(1)(2) + (2)(0) + (2)(1)$.\n\n**Step 2 — Add.** $$2 + 0 + 2 = 4.$$\n\n**Answer.** $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 4$.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "title_markdown": "The magnitude of the vector $\\vec{a} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$ is:",
      "instruction": "Choose the one correct option.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 2,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q2_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "$3$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q2_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "$5$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q2_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "$9$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q2_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$\\sqrt{5}$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q2_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Rule — magnitude.** $$|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{a_x^2 + a_y^2 + a_z^2}.$$\n\n**Step 1 — Square and add components.** $1^2 + 2^2 + 2^2 = 1 + 4 + 4 = 9$.\n\n**Step 2 — Take the square root.** $$|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{9} = 3.$$\n\n**Answer.** $|\\vec{a}| = 3$.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
